From ac1f718fb87bf1c32401ebdf1217ae54777b0ba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mira (mira/mira)" <hey2missmira@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 01:50:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] phase2/fp-walk: allow first-iteration RBP and bound
 monotonic growth
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bound `rbp <= first_rbp` rejected the initial RBP because the loop
starts with `rbp = first_rbp`. Switched to `rbp < first_rbp` so equality
is allowed on the first iteration. After reading the next RBP, break if it
is not strictly greater than the current — that catches broken or looping
chains before they get dereferenced.

Without this fix, the walk added only the leaf RIP (pcs[0]) and stopped,
so observed frames mapped to libc / vdso instead of the test binary.

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
---
 be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_fp_walk.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_fp_walk.cpp b/be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_fp_walk.cpp
index 2b2da291365..cba622321b9 100644
--- a/be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_fp_walk.cpp
+++ b/be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_fp_walk.cpp
@@ -68,8 +68,9 @@ bool rbp_can_read(uintptr_t rbp, uintptr_t first_rbp, long page_size) {
     if ((rbp & (sizeof(uintptr_t) - 1)) != 0) {
         return false;
     }
-    if (rbp <= first_rbp) {
-        // Frame pointers must monotonically grow toward higher addresses.
+    if (rbp < first_rbp) {
+        // Frame pointers walk toward higher addresses; equality is allowed
+        // on the first iteration where rbp == first_rbp.
         return false;
     }
     if (rbp - first_rbp > kMaxStackSpan) {
@@ -123,6 +124,12 @@ void capture_into_slot(const ucontext_t& uc, StackCaptureSlot* out) {
             break;
         }
         out->pcs[n] = return_addr;
+        // The next RBP must be strictly greater than the current one,
+        // else the chain is broken or loops. Stop before dereferencing.
+        if (next_rbp <= rbp) {
+            ++n;
+            break;
+        }
         rbp = next_rbp;
     }
 
